<title>GERMANY: McDonald's plans to expand in Germany.</title>
<headline>McDonald's plans to expand in Germany.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fast-food king McDonald's Corp plans a major expansion of its presence in Germany, opening 400 new restaurants and creating 20,000 new jobs by the year 2000, the head of its German subsidiary said on Friday.</p>
<p>Gerd Raupeter told a gathering to celebrate the 25th anniversery of its presence in Germany the company aimed to boost the number of customers to two million a day from 1.5 million.</p>
<p>McDonald's operates 713 restaurants in Germany and has a workforce of 40,000 employees. Its 1995 turnover in Germany totalled just under three billion marks, he said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
